thub.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T14:40:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T14:40:08Z","body":"> [@matheusmdx](https://github.com/matheusmdx), try https://github.com/json-iterator/test-data/blob/master/large-file.json. I couldn't reproduce it either, but it's causing the permanent freeze. On a low-end device, it may cause a crash\n\nOpening the mentioned JSON is highly probably a crash comes from the system going out of ram to use as to open it here required 4m and almost 11.5GB of ram just for Godot (and 10s to close it and free all the ram). So a system with little ram will have trouble to open a big JSON as this require a lot of ram.\n\n<img width=\"759\" height=\"433\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e167b1cf-bec0-4bf8-a0ff-175436f4a621\" />\n\n\n<br>\n\n-----------------------------\n\n<br>\n\n> > 这根本没用。你需要一个包含调试信息的版本。\n> \n> Where can I download this version?\n\nATM we don't provide executables with debug symbols, they need to be self-compiled. You can see more about here: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/engine_details/development/compiling/index.html\n\n<br>\n\n> [@matheusmdx](https://github.com/matheusmdx) I'm also unable to reproduce this issue. In my project, double-clicking a JSON file in the file system section at the bottom left of the Godot editor causes the entire Godot editor to crash. However, if I create a new project, copy the JSON file into it, and then double-click it, the problem doesn't occur.\n\nYour main project uses any plugin? If you have plugins on the project that crashes its worth attempt to open the JSON file with the plugins disabled.","au