used spine-godot.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4175141825/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4292731250","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116492#issuecomment-4292731250","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116492","id":4292731250,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_3eFy","user":{"login":"fkyah3","id":87884337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODg0MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87884337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3","html_url":"https://github.com/fkyah3","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fkyah3/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-22T00:26:59Z","updated_at":"2026-04-22T00:26:59Z","body":"## Temporary Workaround for Spine Users\n\nI've encountered the same crash (Godot 4.6.1 + Spine GDExtension) and traced the root cause to Spine's EditorImportPlugin claiming the  extension.\n\n**Root Cause**: When Spine GDExtension is loaded, it creates  files for ALL  files in the project — including non-Spine JSON files like level configs, dialogue data, etc. When you double-click such a JSON file in the FileSystem dock, Godot tries to open it with Spine's importer, which crashes when the JSON isn't a valid Spine skeleton.\n\n**Workaround**: I've created a GDScript  plugin that automatically detects and removes these incorrect  files created by Spine:\n\n🔗 **Gist**: https://gist.github.com/fkyah3/814b3310559e3af17b0f1aaa307176ad\n\n**How it works**:\n- Scans all  files on startup and every 10 seconds\n- Checks if the corresponding  contains Spine skeleton keys (, , , etc.)\n- If NOT a Spine skeleton, deletes the  file before it can cause a crash\n- Keeps legitimate Spine skeleton imports intact\n\n**Limitations**:\n- This is a band-aid, not a fix for the underlying Godot/Spine conflict\n- The plugin must remain active; disabling it allows Spine to recreate problematic imports\n- If your Spine skeleton JSON lacks standard keys, it may be incorrectly cleaned\n\nHope this helps other teams hitting the same issue while waiting for an official fix.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4292731250/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]